Torca Island:
{{short description|Phantom island}}
'''Torca Island''' was an inhabited [[phantom island]] said to be located in the [[Indian Ocean]], possibly in the [[East Indies]]. It purportedly vanished when a volcano erupted on 4 June 1693. The survivors escaped to a nearby island called Amboyna (present-day [[Ambon Island]]) on 18 July 1693.<ref>{{cite book|author1=John Wesley|title=A Survey of the Wisdom of God in the Creation: Or a Compendium of Natural Philosophy ... Containing an Abridgment of that Beautiful Work, The Contemplation of Nature, Volume 2|date=1823|publisher=N. Bangs and T. Mason|pages=21–22|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=MRtMAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA21|accessdate=11 January 2023}}</ref> The villagers attempted to flee in canoes or by swimming, but many people died attempting to do this. Torca Island was said to be moderately sized.

