'''Juan de Lisboa''' is a [[phantom island]] in the Western [[Indian Ocean]] allegedly located southeast of [[Madagascar]]. It was reported on maps and [[Nautical chart|charts]] of the 17th and 18th centuries, sometimes depicted alongside another phantom island, Dos Romeiros.<ref>{{cite book |last=Trias |first=Rolando A. Laguarda |date=1988 |title=Pilotos Portugueses en el Rio de la Plata Durante el Siglo XVI |publisher=Instituto de Investigação Científica Tropical |url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Pilotos_Portugueses_en_el_Rio_de_la_Plat/N4ruiK_IJZQC |access-date=October 31, 2026}}</ref>

